  "question": {
    "text": "Two large spherical objects of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> each (uniformly distributed) are fixed as shown in figure. A small point mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is projected from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> heading towards center <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> of second sphere. The minimum velocity of point mass so that it can reach upto second object at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>.&nbsp;Then calculate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>. [Neglect other gravitational forces]<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/hilrwaqvpnvtarzsggmwtyerixtjkwfrrflihroadhcxsmwbeo.jpeg\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "08.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If the ball can reach the mid point of line connecting spheres, then it will get attracted towards B. (At midpoint gravitational intensity is zero)<br />Using energy conservation,<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Solving, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
